---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Tag from '../components/Tag.astro';
import { SOCIALS } from '../consts';

/**
 * The hub page. This is the best structural idea on chrisbarber.co: one tagged
 * table that indexes everything worth reading, wherever it lives — your own
 * posts, your repos, your models, your threads. Add rows over time; a row
 * with an empty tag cell continues the group above it.
 */
---

<Base
    title="Start Here"
    description="The best of Jenish Kothari's work: post-training results, open models and datasets, agentic systems, and research."
>
    <article>
        <h1>Start Here</h1>

        <p>
            I'm Jenish. Software engineer at Adobe, working on post-training. The
            work I care most about is making a small model that runs on one GPU do
            what people currently pay a frontier API to do, and proving it
            with evaluation that <em>executes</em> the output instead of
            string-matching it.
        </p>

        <table class="index-table">
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><Tag tag="post-training" /></td>
                    <td>
                        <a href="https://github.com/jenishk20/finetuning-text-to-sql"
                            >Text-to-SQL on a small model</a
                        >: execution-verified study on Qwen2.5-Coder-7B/14B,
                        benchmarked on BIRD. A 7B ties DeepSeek V4-Pro (1.6T) at
                        roughly 0.4% of the parameters.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td></td>
                    <td>
                        If you're learning DPO: <a
                            href="https://github.com/jenishk20/dpo-text2sql-lab"
                            >DPO Text-to-SQL Lab</a
                        >: six notebooks from <code>y = 3x + 2</code> up to
                        DPO on real preference pairs.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td></td>
                    <td>
                        If you're learning GRPO: <a
                            href="https://github.com/jenishk20/grpo-text-2-sql"
                            >grpo-text-2-sql</a
                        >: the SQL executor <em>is</em> the reward function, so
                        there's no reward model and no preference pairs to build.
                    </td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><Tag tag="local" /></td>
                    <td>
                        <a href="https://huggingface.co/jk200201/qwen2.5-coder-7b-bird-cot"
                            >qwen2.5-coder-7b-bird-cot</a
                        >: reasoning-distilled text-to-SQL model.
                        <a
                            href="https://huggingface.co/jk200201/qwen2.5-coder-7b-bird-cot-GGUF"
                            >GGUF build</a
                        > for local inference.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td></td>
                    <td>
                        <a href="https://huggingface.co/spaces/jk200201/text2sql-live"
                            >LocalSQL</a
                        >: ask a question, get SQL, run it live.
                    </td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><Tag tag="evals" /></td>
                    <td>
                        Datasets: <a
                            href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/jk200201/bird-cot-sft"
                            >bird-cot-sft</a
                        > (CoT traces distilled from Qwen3-Coder-480B),
                        <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/jk200201/spider-dpo-1040"
                            >spider-dpo-1040</a
                        > (1,040 execution-verified preference pairs).
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td></td>
                    <td>
                        <a href="https://github.com/jenishk20/sql-agent-rl-env"
                            >sql-agent-rl-env</a
                        >: the RL environment for SQL agents.
                    </td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><Tag tag="agents" /></td>
                    <td>
                        <a href="https://github.com/jenishk20/package-quarantine"
                            >package-quarantine</a
                        >: detonates dependencies in a honeypot sandbox before
                        your coding agent installs them.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td></td>
                    <td>
                        <a href="https://github.com/jenishk20/MedSignal">MedSignal</a>
                        is local-first clinical intelligence, running entirely
                        on-device.
                    </td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><Tag tag="systems" /></td>
                    <td>
                        <a href="https://github.com/jenishk20/drift-sentinel"
                            >Drift Sentinel</a
                        >: catches the schema changes that quietly degrade ML
                        models without breaking any pipeline.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td></td>
                    <td>
                        <a href="https://github.com/jenishk20/splitwise-splitter"
                            >SplitMate</a
                        >: receipt photos to itemized group splits. 22+ users,
                        $23K+ split across 182+ receipts.
                    </td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><Tag tag="research" /></td>
                    <td>
                        <strong>Automatic Highlight Generation</strong>, IEEE ICAD 2026.
                        <a
                            href="https://github.com/jenishk20/Automatic-Highlight-Generation"
                            >paper repo</a
                        >. 82% accuracy, 88% recall on goal detection; condenses a
                        90-minute match in under 15 minutes.
                    </td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td><Tag tag="interviews" /></td>
                    <td>
                        <a href="/interviews/">The interview log</a>: every loop
                        I have done in the US, what stage it reached, and how it
                        ended.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td></td>
                    <td>
                        <a href="/four-rounds-at-amazon-seattle-hq/"
                            >Four rounds at Amazon's Seattle HQ, then nothing</a
                        >. Flew out, four rounds, and the recruiter stopped
                        replying.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td></td>
                    <td>
                        <a href="/five-rounds-at-deepinfra/"
                            >Five rounds at DeepInfra, and a reason</a
                        >. The same outcome, handled the opposite way.
                    </td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <p>
            Everything else is on <a href={SOCIALS.github}>GitHub</a> and
            <a href={SOCIALS.huggingface}>Hugging Face</a>. Most responsive contact:
            <a href={SOCIALS.x}>X DMs</a>.
        </p>
    </article>
</Base>
